            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and evaluation of 4-substituted benzylamine derivatives as beta-tryptase inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2986-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Since beta-tryptase is considered a critical mediator of asthma, potent tryptase inhibitors may be useful as new agents for the treatment of asthma. We investigated 4-substituted benzylamine derivatives and obtained M58539 (15h) as a potent inhibitor of beta-tryptase (IC50 = 5.0 nM) with high selectivity against other serine proteases, low molecular weight, clog P value less than 5, lack of amidino and guanidino groups, and independence of Zn2+ ion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
